@ [detected_utc] 2026-08-28T15:47:23.2556579Z

& [Fault]
  + recursive evidence verification treated every artifact path as repository-root relative
  + thirty-five retained artifact references in current manifests are intentionally manifest-directory relative and therefore failed with an absent repository-root file before stale-state accounting
  + directory-local manifests use a closed SHA256 object with algorithm and value while repository-wide manifests use a scalar hash and the recursive verifier previously understood only the scalar form

& [Containment]
  + the refusal was deterministic and no manifest or evidence artifact was silently skipped or rewritten
  + no provider model process network remote activation cleanup or foreign work was contacted

& [Correction]
  + resolve an artifact against the repository root first and only when that regular file is absent resolve it against the containing manifest directory
  + retain absolute-path and parent-traversal refusal and convert resolved nested-manifest dependencies back to canonical repository-relative identities before recursion
  + explicitly read and preserve both the scalar SHA256 and lowercase algorithm-value SHA256 forms while refusing every other shape
  + rewrite and retimestamp only manifests whose artifact identity actually changed so a scoped refresh does not create unrelated evidence churn

& [Evidence]
  + current inventory contains 2424 repository-root-only references thirty-five manifest-local-only references one deterministic root-precedence overlap and zero missing references
  + verify-only replay must complete with zero stale references after intentional NHC-02 transitive hash refresh
